<title>GERMANY: WAIGEL REJECTS CRITICISM OF BUBA MONETARY POLICY.</title>
<headline>WAIGEL REJECTS CRITICISM OF BUBA MONETARY POLICY.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel on Friday rejected criticism of the monetary policies of Bundesbank and said economic growth and jobs could not be achieved through targeted exchange rate policies.</p>
<p>Waigel's statements come a day after a member of the Bank of France council attacked the Bundesbank, saying devalution of the French franc against the mark could be necessary because of German incomprehension on monetary and exchange rate policy.</p>
</text>
